58
00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.162
Stadium.

59
00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:46.919
Whistle.

60
00:02:47.619 --> 00:02:51.058
Whistle means a small thing you blow to make a high sound.

61
00:02:51.358 --> 00:02:53.091
The game started with a whistle.

62
00:02:53.791 --> 00:02:55.990
Your turn. Say: Whistle.

63
00:02:58.690 --> 00:02:59.413
Whistle.

64
00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:02.254
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:02.554 --> 00:03:04.832
Sreypich, did your team play last week?

66
00:03:06.117 --> 00:03:08.360
Yes, we played in the school tournament.

67
00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:10.698
Did you win?

68
00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:14.738
We won the first game, but we lost the final.

69
00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.099
Never mind! Who scored?

70
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:21.801
I scored one goal, and everyone cheered!

71
00:03:23.117 --> 00:03:26.405
Grammar focus: Past simple (regular verbs).

72
00:03:26.705 --> 00:03:29.288
We practiced yesterday. We won the game.

73
00:03:29.588 --> 00:03:34.887
Regular verbs add -ed in the past. Win and lose are irregular: won, lost.

74
00:03:35.883 --> 00:03:38.582
Now read and listen. The Big Tournament.

75
00:03:38.882 --> 00:03:41.125
Our school team practices every week.

76
00:03:42.417 --> 00:03:45.403
Last week, we played in a big tournament at the stadium.

77
00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:49.157
Our coach shouted, and the fans cheered for us.

78
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.320
We won the first match, but we lost the final.

79
00:03:54.617 --> 00:03:57.615
We were a little sad, but we were proud of our teamwork.

80
00:03:58.917 --> 00:04:01.615
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

81
00:04:01.915 --> 00:04:03.648
We blank football yesterday.

82
00:04:03.948 --> 00:04:07.160
A, play. B, played. C, plays.

83
00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.894
The answer is B: played.

84
00:04:14.383 --> 00:04:16.650
The person who controls a match is the blank.

85
00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:20.092
A, referee. B, coach. C, fan.

86
00:04:24.083 --> 00:04:26.478
The answer is A: referee.

87
00:04:27.983 --> 00:04:30.180
Last week, our team blank the cup!

88
00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:33.437
A, win. B, won. C, winned.

89
00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:39.217
The answer is B: won.

90
00:04:40.717 --> 00:04:44.158
Now it's your turn to speak. What sport do you enjoy playing?

91
00:04:49.458 --> 00:04:55.559
I enjoy playing volleyball. Last month, my team played in a competition, and we won two games.

92
00:04:55.859 --> 00:04:57.650
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

93
00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:03.322
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and past simple (regular verbs).

94
00:05:03.622 --> 00:05:07.192
Today's value is teamwork. We can do more when we work together.

95
00:05:07.492 --> 00:05:09.703
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

96
00:05:10.003 --> 00:05:12.655
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

